squad-new-role-plan-390 examples :: ["How the squad works: worked examples Rank. You are a 74 rated striker and the club's forwards are 80, 74, 71, 69 and 65. 2 of them are rated 74 or more (a tie goes to the other 74), so on our ratings you are 3rd of 6 forwards: the last one into the front three. Trust. At a club whose squad level is 72, a 74 is 2 above it. The plan for that is 20 to 30 league games, and 25 of 38 is trust 66%. A dressing room that has your back adds 2 games: 71%. A thin season. At 62 in that same squad you are 10 under the level and 6th of 6 forwards on our ratings. The plan for that is 8 to 18 league games, and Last season tells you why. Form. Last season at this club you played 24 league games and rated 7.8. A plan of 20 to 30 games becomes 22 to 32 before dressing room effects, injuries or a freeze. The same appearances with a 6.2 rating make it 18 to 28. At a new club neither result carries over."]
